Accessing OS:
Accessing OS can be done in 2 ways.
    1.Console(Physical machine UI, ie connecting monitor to CPU using HDMI cable). We can access anything in UI
    2.Remote(Connecting you OS or machine remotely over network)
        1.Connecting remote windows OS from host windows OS, can be done using RDP.
        2.Connect windows(host) to linux through remote can done using putty client.From Windows 10 onwards, we can connect one windows OS to linux by cmd prompt using ssh. eg ssh ip(linux machine ip)
        3.Connect one linux machine to another linux machine can done using ssh. eg ssh ip(another or remote machine ip)

Putty:
Used to connect from windows system to linux system remotely

Access Linux System through putty or through ssh:
    1.Through Putty:
        1. Open putty give ip then give username and password.You will be login to the linux machine remotely through CLI interface
            - Getting IP address of linux machine(centOS)
            - For CentOS till 7.5 we can use ifconfig
            - But for centos >= 7.5 use ip addr.Still you want to use ifconfig the need to install yum install net-tools
            - When we give ifconfig to fetch ip , always take ip from enpos3

    2. Through ssh:
        1. In windows 10, we can connect to linux system remotely through ssh accessing from command prompt instead of putty.
        2. Open cmd and type ssh -l username ip or ssh ip .Here -l user to represent username. Then enter username and password which take you to linux CLI

