 FileSystem:
 OS use filesystem to store files and directory.Where we manage and access files.In linux filesystem everything stored in folder structure. Like windows, C driver is the root directory, inside we have program files which store application installable, user folder which has user directory and Windows folder have OS related files. Same way in Linux cd / where / is home directory like C drive. Which have folder structures.
 cd /  - will take us to root directory
 ls -l  - list all directories
 Example below
 etc - Store configuration file
 var - log file
 home - user directories
 We can remember this by taking example of cupboard, where in cupboard shirts placed in some row, shoes in some row, jewels in some row etc. like that linux file system have folder structure to store files.

File System Structures and descriptions:
/ is the root directory like c drive.
cd / will go to that directory
ls -l will list the directory

/boot - will have boot loader file ie grub.cfg. Which has which OS and it version etc.When we start the machine,based on this file only system starts up
/root - this has all root user files and directory
/dev - which has all the peripheral(keyboard, mouse etc) files
/etc - all application configuration files present inside here. eg DNS config file
/bin --> /usr/bin - all user command files. like top, ls, pwd etc
/sbin --> /usr/sbin - all system/filesystem command files. This will be used when we increase the file system and change filesystem configurations
/opt - which have third party application installed like oracle .Not OS related apps
/proc - All current running process file.When system shutdown all files will be cleared
/lib --> /usr/lib - Have library file of all the command.Like top command will have library file and all command will be written in C and C++. All command related library will stored here.
    - To see which library are associated for each command strace -e open top
/home - will have user directory
/tmp -  will have all temporary files
/var - will have all application log files inside var /log will have all log files
/run - will have all running app pid files
/mnt - it used to mount external filesystem to current system
/media - In computer we have cd drive. if we attach CD in that drive, that content will be stored here.

