Difference between ls and ls -l:
ls - will just list the file and directory
ls -l will list the properties of the files and directory
Property say like what are names of files and directory we have, with it size , who created , when last accessed, what group it associated. In windows if we right click file or folder to see the properties which show all details of file or folder, same is ls -l
In ls -l , the output start with d means its directory, - means file and l means links
Output of ls -l
lrwxrwxrwx.   1 root root    7 Nov 17 11:03 bin -> usr/bin
drwxr-xr-x.  20 root root 3200 Nov 20 20:41 dev
-rw-------. 1 root   root        0 Nov 17 11:15 yum.log
drwxr-xr-x - Directory, 20 is how many folder we have inside with parent directory of dev, root is who created, root is which group, 3200 is size, Nov 20 20:41 is time it got created, dev is directory name
lrwxrwxrwx - which is link, rest same
-rw------- -  Which is file, rest same

