Soft and Hard links
inode - all file which we created will have a number and that number only will get stored in harddisk. whenever we are retrieving the file, it will retrieve in backend based on number
Soft link:
When we create a file and we create a softlink for that, and if we remove or rename that file the softlink also will get deleted
Create file:
touch test
Soft link cannot created in same directory, so creating softlink in /tmp
cd /tmp
ln -s /home/drajendran/test - softlink will be created. -s is softlink
if we delete the orginal file in /home/drajendran/test softlink will not get access to it

Hard link:
When we create a file and we create a Hardlink for that, and if we remove or rename that file the hardlink also will not get deleted
Create file:
touch test
Hard link cannot created in same directory, so creating hardlink in /tmp
cd /tmp
ln /home/drajendran/test - hardlink will be created. -s is not for hardlink
if we delete the orginal file in /home/drajendran/test hardlink will get access to it

ls -ltri - used to get inode number i is inode

